## SQ-TER-06 | ocean geodes covered in the floor block (floorPatch SWAP)
> execute positioned 0 70 0 run locate biome minecraft:deep_ocean
waitlog nearest minecraft:deep_ocean is at 300
capture GO is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
> chunky center {GO1} {GO3}
> chunky radius 300
> chunky start
waitlog Task finished 1800
> zq count {GO1-300} 20 {GO3-300} {GO1-150} 63 {GO3-150} minecraft:calcite
> zq count {GO1-150} 20 {GO3-150} {GO1} 63 {GO3} minecraft:calcite
> zq count {GO1} 20 {GO3} {GO1+150} 63 {GO3+150} minecraft:calcite
> zq count {GO1-300} 20 {GO3-300} {GO1+300} 63 {GO3+300} minecraft:amethyst_block
> zq count {GO1-300} 20 {GO3-300} {GO1+300} 63 {GO3+300} minecraft:smooth_basalt
look zq "count" lines give the blocks and "on:" what they stand on; calcite and smooth basalt seen from the water (first block below water) should be about 0: fly 5 geode spots in the client block for the look (ST-305); prismarine geodes untouched. zq count reads loaded chunks only: run right after Chunky while they are still loaded, else forceload the box first

